# Syntax baseline: ES5 (IE 11 is the last ES5-only browser).
# This file is consumed by @babel/preset-env (babel.config.js, useBuiltIns: 'usage' + core-js 3) to inject polyfills
# on demand, and by autoprefixer to generate CSS vendor prefixes.
# Note: do not use `not dead` — it would drop legacy WebView/Safari versions that are no longer updated from the target set.
# Runtime caveat: Vue 3 relies on Proxy (not polyfillable), which is only supported from Chrome 49 onward,
# so the app can only actually run on Chrome 49+. `ie 11` here is a pure *syntax* floor: it forces Babel — and the
# webpack runtime, which derives its output syntax from browserslist when a config exists — to emit ES5-only syntax.
# Side effect: core-js will inject ES5-era polyfills (Symbol/Promise/WeakMap/...) that are unused on Chrome 49+,
# which slightly grows the bundle in exchange for maximum syntax compatibility.

ie 11
